  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hi, the light in my Neff oven has stopped working (model B1ACE4HN0B). Oven works fine otherwise. Can I change the bulb myself and what bulb do I need?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Blown oven light bulb]\nYes, you can replace the bulb yourself. For your Neff model B1ACE4HN0B, you need a 25W, 230V heat-resistant glass bulb with an SES (small Edison screw/E14) cap. These are rated for high temperatures (usually up to 300°C or 600°F). 1. Ensure the oven is switched off and cool.\n2. Unscrew the old bulb carefully (it may be hot if used recently).\n3. Screw in the new heat-resistant SES/E14 bulb. If you buy a standard household bulb, it will likely blow very quickly or even shatter due to the heat inside the oven cavity."
  }
